# Implementation Plan - Restructure Frontend & Integrate High-Fidelity Stitch Screens

This plan details the modularization of the React frontend in `project/frontend/src` and the integration of the four high-fidelity screens from the Stitch enterprise design workspace.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Iconography**: The downloaded Stitch screens utilize Google's Material Symbol font icons. We will map these to standard Lucide React SVG-based icons (`lucide-react`) to match the rest of the application's React styling ecosystem and ensure fast, offline-compatible rendering.
> - **Simulated Prototypes**: The downloaded screens contain visual loading animations (e.g., table skeleton, scanner line, chart bar transitions). We will implement these animations using Tailwind CSS utility classes and local component state.

## Proposed Changes

We will extract the monolithic tabs inside [App.tsx](file:///d:/vibe%20code/spend-managment/project/frontend/src/App.tsx) and place them in their respective feature folders under `src/features/` and `src/components/`.

